{"text": "Dorothy lived in the middle of the great Kansas prairies with Uncle Henry and Aunt Em. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Uncle Henry was a farmer, and Aunt Em was his wife. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Their house was small because the wood for it had to be carried by wagon many miles. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> It had four walls, a floor, and a roof, which made one room. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> In this room there were a rusty cookstove, a cupboard for the dishes, a table, and some chairs. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Uncle Henry and Aunt Em had a big bed in one corner, and Dorothy had a little bed in another. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Under the floor there was a small, dark hole that the family called a cyclone cellar. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The family could go there when one of those great whirlwinds came. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> A trap door in the middle of the floor led down to it. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> When Dorothy stood in the doorway, she could see nothing but the great gray prairie. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The sun had baked the plowed land into a gray mass with little cracks. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Once the house had been painted, but now it was as dull and gray as everything else.", "alignment": {"characters": ["D", "o", "r", "o", "t", "h", "y", " ", "l", "i", "v", "e", "d", " ", "i", "n", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "m", "i", "d", "d", "l", "e", " ", "o", "f", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "g", "r", "e", "a", "t", " ", "K", "a", "n", "s", "a", "s", " ", "p", "r", "a", "i", "r", "i", "e", "s", " ", "w", "i", "t", "h", " ", "U", "n", "c", "l", "e", " ", "H", "e", "n", "r", "y", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "A", "u", "n", "t", " ", "E", "m", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", "=", "\"", "0", ".", "8", "s", "\"", " ", "/", ">", " ", "U", "n", "c", "l", "e", " ", "H", "e", "n", "r", "y", " ", "w", "a", "s", " ", "a", " ", "f", "a", "r", "m", "e", "r", ",", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "A", "u", "n", "t", " ", "E", "m", " ", "w", "a", "s", " ", "h", "i", "s",